 tumors, except for prolactinomas which may be managed medically if there is no urgent deterioration of vision.", "runs": [{"text": "This is the primary treatment for most symptomatic pituitary tumors, except for prolactinomas which may be managed medically if there is no urgent deterioration of vision."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "400"}}, {"id": "body-25545", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Trans-sphenoidal approach (endoscopic or microsurgical) is preferred as it is safer and better tolerated.", "runs": [{"text": "Trans-sphenoidal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "approach"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(endoscopic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "microsurgical)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "preferred"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "as"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "it"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "safer"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "better"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tolerated."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "400"}}, {"id": "body-25546", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Frequently subtotal especially in large tumors or tumors invading into cavernous sinuses. Hypopituitarism occurs post- operative in about 12% of patients.", "runs": [{"text": "Frequently"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "subtotal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "especially"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "large"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tumors"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tumors"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "invading"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "into"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cavernous"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sinuses."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Hypopituitarism occurs"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "post- operative in about 12% of patients."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "400"}}, {"id": "body-25548", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Radiotherapy", "runs": [{"text": "Radiotherapy"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-25549", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Indicated post subtotal tumor resection, recurrent tumors, persistently elevated circulating hormone levels, and inoperable patients.", "runs": [{"text": "Indicated post subtotal tumor resection, recurrent tumors, persistently elevated circulating hormone levels, and inoperable"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patients."}]}, {"id": "body-25550", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Follow up MRI 3 months after surgery to assess residual tumor.", "runs": [{"text": "Follow"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "up"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "MRI"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "3"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "months"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "after"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "surgery"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "assess"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "residual"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tumor."}]}, {"id": "body-25552", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Radiotherapy is very effective for control of growth of pituitary tumors (>95%), but less effective for decreasing circulating hormone levels in functional tumors.", "runs": [{"text": "Radiotherapy"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "very"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "effective"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "control"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "growth"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pituitary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tumors"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(>95%),"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "but"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "less"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "effective"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "decreasing"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "circulating hormone levels in functional tumors."}]}, {"id": "body-25554", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Common complications", "runs": [{"text": "Common"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "complications"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-25555", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Diabetes Insipidus: is characterized by excessive urine output due to lack of ADH, usually immediate post-operative but may be delayed. Patient will present with Polyuria, Polydipsia and some of them Polyphagia. In immediate post-operative period you may consider fluid replacement (monitoring in input, output and serum electrolyte). Consider medical treatment if not resolving", "runs": [{"text": "Diabetes", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Insipidus:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "characterized"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "excessive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "urine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "output"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "due"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "lack"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ADH,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "usually"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "immediate"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "post-operative"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "but"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may be delayed. Patient will present with Polyuria, Polydipsia and some of them Polyphagia. In immediate post-operative period you may consider fluid replacement (monitoring in input, output and serum electrolyte). Consider medical treatment if not "}, {"text": "resolving"}]}, {"id": "body-25557", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "S: desmopressin (PO) 0.05mg 12 hourly daily (titrate based on response.", "runs": [{"text": "S:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "desmopressin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "0.05mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "12"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hourly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "daily"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(titrate"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "based"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "on"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "response."}]}, {"id": "body-25558", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "OR", "runs": [{"text": "OR"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-25559", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "S: tolvaptan 7.5mg (PO) maximum dose 30mg in 24hr.", "runs": [{"text": "S:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "tolvaptan"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "7.5mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "maximum"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dose"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "30mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "24hr."}]}, {"id": "body-25561", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone Secretion (SIADH) is characterized by decreased urine output and hyponatremia due to excessive ADH secretion, may occur early (first week) or late (2nd week) post operative. It’s important to note that SIADH may occur in TBI, Brain tumors, CNS infections and some medications, treat the cause and manage hyponatremia according the guideline on electrolyte imbalance section.", "runs": [{"text": "Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone Secretion (SIADH) ", "bold": true}, {"text": "is characterized by decreased urine output and hyponatremia"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "due"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "excessive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ADH"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "secretion,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "occur"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "early"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(first"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "week)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "late"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(2nd"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "week)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "post"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "operative."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "It’s"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "important"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to note that SIADH may occur in TBI, Brain tumors, CNS infections and some medications, treat the cause and manage hyponatremia according the guideline on electrolyte imbalance section."}]}, {"id": "body-25563", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "A: furosemide (PO/IV) 40mg Once or twice a day", "runs": [{"text": "A:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "furosemide"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO/IV)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "40mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Once"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "twice"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "day"}]}, {"id": "body-25564", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "AND/OR", "runs": [{"text": "AND/OR"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-25565", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "S: tolvaptan 7.5mg (PO) maximum dose 30mg in 24hr", "runs": [{"text": "S:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "tolvaptan"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "7.5mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "maximum"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dose"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "30mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "24hr"}]}, {"id": "body-25567", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Cerebral Salt Wasting(CSW): characterized by excessive urine sodium secretion and hyponatremia, usually immediate post- operative. Manage hyponatremia with", "runs": [{"text": "Cerebral", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Salt", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Wasting(CSW):", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "characterized"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "excessive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "urine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sodium"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "secretion"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hyponatremia,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "usually"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "immediate"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "post- operative. Manage hyponatremia with"}]}, {"id": "body-25568", "type": "paragraph", "style":